WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Connect your institutional MATLAB license for an ISSM cloud run.
Why: Keep the source inputs, inspect native fields, and save a complete result package.
Look for: Have your own port@server address and an approved connected cloud account ready.

2
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Start here in CryoLauncher. Choose Cloud for this tutorial.
Why: Your workspace keeps scripts, dataset references and results together.
Look for: Your workspace keeps scripts, datasets, run history and results together.

3
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Choose Cloud and ISSM; find MATLAB LICENSE.
Why: Choose the intended interface, model and example before editing or launching a run.
Look for: Your cloud account connection must already be verified.

4
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Already configured? Prepare the local reference for reattachment.
Why: This recovery reattaches the existing license reference without overwriting its value.
Look for: Save the current ARN privately; first-ever license entry skips this conditional step.

5
00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Paste your own institutional address into the masked license field.
Why: The institutional license address stays masked and must be reachable for the native run.
Look for: Keep license values and secret references out of shared recordings.

6
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Check the masked license input.
Why: The institutional license address stays masked and must be reachable for the native run.
Look for: Use the port@server address provided by your institution.

7
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Choose Configure license.
Why: This recovery reattaches the existing license reference without overwriting its value.
Look for: This recovery finds the existing managed secret and reattaches its access.

8
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Wait for MATLAB license configured and the input to clear.
Why: This recovery reattaches the existing license reference without overwriting its value.
Look for: The typed value does not overwrite this existing secret’s stored value.

9
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:45.000
Make the private license service reachable from your Connector host.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: Off campus, establish the institution’s required VPN first.

10
00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:54.000
Choose Open Connector.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: Use the same signed-in user in the application and Connector.

11
00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:04.000
Start the application’s Connector pairing request.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: The next view resumes with the one-time code hidden.

12
00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:16.000
In the external Connector, enter your own current pairing code.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: Keep the Connector and required network connection running during the job.

13
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:25.000
After pairing, choose Re-check.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: This checks connectivity; it does not execute MATLAB.

14
00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:37.000
Wait for CryoStack Connector connected.
Why: The Connector gives the cloud job access to a private institutional license service.
Look for: The same-user bridge is online for the native run.

15
00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Open Review & Launch and confirm ISSM runtime is Ready.
Why: Review confirms the intended model, source, resources and charges before submission.
Look for: Review the account, model, resources, time limit and estimated charges.

16
00:02:49.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Verify the license path with the completed native ISSM run.
Why: A completed native job and its recorded provenance provide execution evidence.
Look for: MATLAB R2024b Update 7 · ISSM 2026.1 · native exit code 0.

17
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:15.000
Keep the license reference private and retain the run provenance.
Why: Keep the scientific input definitions and numerical qualifications with the result.
Look for: This guide reattaches an existing secret; conditional reset, VPN and external entry are explained.
